      "adaptations": [
        {
          "kind": "power",
          "note": "One tag-team encounter for the client's two hero cards (LOOTA_BOSS_15h George and Karl with Divinity, LOOTA_BOSS_32h Karl and George with The Silver Hand). As the wiki's Dungeon Run table states (\"30 HP each. Starts with George and switches to Karl on defeat\"; round 6 only), each of the two has its own 30 Health: Tag Team swaps the active hero with the benched one, each keeping its own damage, and when the active one is defeated the other takes over if it still stands. Armor, the weapon and the board stay with the side; the hero power is fresh after a swap, as after every hero power replacement. Tag Team does nothing once the benched hero is defeated."
        },
        {
          "kind": "health",
          "note": "Identity Health: 30 for each of the two heroes at every floor (the wiki: 30 HP each, where most round 6 bosses have 50), so fixedHealth; the act curve and the modifiers' bossHealthDelta do not apply."
        },
        {
          "kind": "power",
          "note": "Divinity is not offered when every minion of the boss has Divine Shield already (it would do nothing)."
        }
      ],
      "modifierReasons": {
        "mod_iron_bosses": "the row's Health is its identity (fixedHealth: DungeonRun.BossHealth ignores bossHealthDelta), so Iron Bosses' +5 never reaches the fight; a stamp-4 schedule neutralises the modifier for this fight only (DungeonRun.NeutraliseKnobs; its extra treasure after a major is kept), a released one bans it for the act",
        "mod_open_road": "the row's Health is its identity (fixedHealth), so Open Road's +3 boss Health never reaches the fight and only its extra opening card would; a stamp-4 schedule neutralises the modifier for this fight only (no extra card), a released one bans it for the act"
      },
      "v4": {
        "incompatibleModifiers": [
          "mod_iron_bosses",
          "mod_open_road"
        ]
      }
